// A non-`void` function must produce its declared return type on every path (E0048). This one
// declares `: int` but its body ends in a bare expression, so control falls off the end and the
// function would implicitly return `unit` where `int` was promised — a soundness hole rejected
// statically, before either backend runs. Only a `void` function may fall off the end. The error
// points at the function name.
// expect: error E0048 at 8:4
// expect: exit 1
fn double(n: int): int {
    n + n
}
echo double(21)
